 "This bell is an example of early American craftsmanship. It is made of solid copper and features a intricate pattern of engravings on the surface. The bell is marked with what appears to be a maker's mark, 'JS&S', which is believed to be the initials of the silversmith who crafted it. The bell is also stamped with the date '1799', indicating that it was made during the late 18th century."

How many words are in the museum note?

A) 56
B) 58
C) 60
D) 62

